From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:33:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/34] surface coherent: a CPU write opens the whole surface

A write costs a probe of every tracked surface before its page is known. A CPU
writer going down a surface paid that once a page: MercuryPosterExtension's
alpha fill stopped at every page of the wallpaper. The first write now holds
and snapshots every page and opens them all, so a writer stops once, and the
copy in takes the whole surface. The ledger pays for it.

Pages::probe is new: it is what names a write's page now that held pages are
read-only, and arm alone cannot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
