 //!
-//! **A CPU write** never loses to a sync. The write stops before it lands, so the page's snapshot
-//! is what the guest overwrote: a later sync over the open page keeps every texel that differs
-//! from the snapshot ([`Coherent::merge`]). A GPU copy back over an open page cannot merge, so
+//! **A CPU write** never loses to a sync. The write stops before it lands, and opens the whole
+//! surface: a CPU writer covers it page by page, and each page would cost a probe of every surface.
+//! So each page's snapshot is what the guest overwrote: a later sync over the open pages keeps
+//! every texel that differs from it ([`Coherent::merge`]). A GPU copy back over an open page cannot merge, so
 //! [`Coherent::before_flush`] waits for the records, a bounded time, and syncs on the CPU; past
 //! the bound it counts `overwrite_risk`. Writing also demotes the surface to the shadow's own keep
 //! and merge.
@@ -121,8 +122,13 @@ pub trait Pages: Send + Sync {
     /// Armed pages, and open ones with `open_too`, held; the pages a CPU may have reached as the
